cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Semantic Fact Database (SFDB): A Sheaf-Inspired Database for Contextual Semantic Facts"
authors:
  - alias: "BlackSamuron0305"
abstract: >
  A prototype context-indexed semantic fact database. Facts are stored as
  sections over a finite poset of contexts and retrieved through
  stalk-indexed lookup rather than triple reconstruction. A companion
  reified triple-store baseline (with a dict-indexed storage-layer control
  variant) is provided over the same canonical schema, and three-way
  cross-engine semantic equivalence is verified for every query. In
  benchmarks at up to 100,000 facts, SFDB is 18-34x faster than the KG
  baseline on entity-anchored LOOKUP queries, 37-102x faster on unrestricted
  GLOBAL scans, and 2.8-4.1x faster on context-scoped CONTEXT queries, with
  most of each advantage surviving a storage-layer control that isolates it
  from the cost of SQLite round trips. Insert throughput and temporal-range
  queries do not favour SFDB unconditionally: SFDB is slower than KG at the
  smallest scale on inserts, and the temporal-range advantage does not
  survive the storage-layer control at all -- SFDB is at parity or slower
  than the control on bounded temporal ranges at most scales. The cost that
  funds the advantages that do hold is memory: SFDB uses roughly 1-2.8x
  more resident memory per fact than the KG baseline. All of this is
  reported as measured rather than smoothed into a single directional
  claim; see the paper (paper/main.pdf) for the full evaluation.
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-08"
repository-code: "https://github.com/BlackSamuron0305/semantic-fact-db"
url: "https://github.com/BlackSamuron0305/semantic-fact-db"
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - "semantic database"
  - "knowledge graph"
  - "presheaf"
  - "context-indexed storage"
  - "cross-engine equivalence"
